  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is running hot and building real momentum; Hicksville is overperforming its calendar expectation but flagging a retention risk you need to address.\n\nPort Washington delivered $4,079 yesterday with six groomers producing $564 per groomer\u201411% above your trailing-30-day baseline. Week-to-date you're +18% in revenue on +17% appointments, and your MTD number of $76.2K beats the DOW-adjusted expectation by 2.4%, meaning the team is executing, not just catching a favorable calendar. The one operational miss: add-on attach collapsed to 42% from 71% last Thursday. That's real upsell discipline slippage\u2014flag it with Danielle and your grooming leads. Retail is solid at +8%. Year-to-date you're +50% in revenue and +52% in appointments versus last year; this is the store that's carrying growth.\n\nHicksville surprised yesterday with 73% revenue growth on 80% more transactions, and $25.6K MTD is +9.9% versus the DOW-adjusted expectation\u2014real outperformance. Add-on attach jumped to 47% and retail spiked 122%, so front-of-house and upsell are both firing. But buried in the data is a problem: your 12+ week visit-gap bucket grew from 8.4% to 10.2% in the last reporting period. Customers are stretching out. Combined with only 2\u20133 groomers scheduled through the next week, you're at genuine risk of stealth churn. The lapse pool of 58 customers is small but represents $40K in annual value\u2014you need a reactivation push now before the gap widens further.\n\nBoth stores have inventory gaps on core products (X-Small Treat Table is backorder at both locations; bully sticks are negative stock). Reorder immediately. Today: Port Washington 6 groomer(s) and 7.0h bathers; Hicksville 2 groomer(s) and 0.0h bathers. Next 7 days: Port Washington 29 groomer-days, Hicksville 11 groomer-days\u2014capacity disparity is real and matches the retention risk signal at Hicksville."
